    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "`RateLimiter` is implemented in `solution.py` to the spec, and the 14 tests I wrote in `tests/test_solution.py` pass. I didn't run a coverage check, so I can't confirm the 90% gate. The tests do exercise every method and every error path.\n\nEach client keeps a list of accepted requests with their times and costs, and expired ones are dropped on each call. `retry_after` walks the client's active requests oldest-first and returns the wait until enough of them expire for the cost to fit. The tests also check that rejected requests record nothing, clients are independent, a request exactly `window_seconds` old no longer counts, and a `now` earlier than any seen so far raises `ValueError`.\n\nThe spec doesn't say which check wins when a call has both a bad `cost` and a backwards `now`, so a bad `cost` is checked first. Either way the call raises `ValueError`.",
